==================================================================
 THE SAME BUSINESS, CUT THREE WAYS
==================================================================

  cells   per cell   threshold   quiet run   planted z   found?
  -----   --------   ---------   ---------   ---------   ------
  24      500        3.49        0 cleared   -14.64      YES
  240     50         3.77        0 cleared   -5.19       YES
  1200    10         4.11        1 cleared   -3.34       no  (S838 cleared instead)

  Fifty times the search width buys an 18% higher bar. The
  Bonferroni correction is the CHEAP part -- it grows like the
  square root of a logarithm and it was never going to dominate
  anything. What collapses is the planted cell's z, and it
  collapses because the cell it lives in has almost nothing in it.

==================================================================
 WHAT A CHANGE WOULD HAVE HAD TO BE, TO BE FOUND
==================================================================

  cells   a typical cell bills   smallest detectable change
  -----   --------------------   --------------------------
  24      635515                 113554        (18% of a cell)
  240     65011                  34303         (53% of a cell)
  1200    12349                  18096         (147% of a cell)

  Read the last row twice. At twelve hundred cells the smallest
  change that could clear the bar is larger than a typical cell's
  entire revenue, so NO DECLINE IN SUCH A CELL, HOWEVER COMPLETE,
  COULD EVER BE REPORTED. The cell could go to zero and the answer
  would still be `within ordinary variation` -- in exactly the
  words the library uses when a business is healthy.

==================================================================
 WHAT THIS MEASURED
==================================================================

  1. THE PREDICTION WAS WRONG, AND IN A USEFUL DIRECTION. Search
     width does not dominate. Widening the search fifty-fold moves
     the threshold from 3.49 to 4.11, because sqrt(2 ln n) grows
     about as slowly as anything in statistics. Paying for the
     multiplicity of a wide search is nearly free.

  2. WHAT DOMINATES IS SUPPORT. Cut the same business finer and
     each cell holds less of it, so each cell's ordinary variation
     grows relative to its size. The planted cell loses 75% of its
     revenue in all three runs and its z falls from -14.6 to -3.3.
     Nothing about that cell changed between the runs; only how
     much of the business was left in it.

  3. AND THE LIBRARY HAD NO WAY TO SAY SO. `within ordinary
     variation` is returned identically by a search that examined a
     healthy business and by one that could not have found a cell
     going to zero. That silence is what R15 fixes: a Finding now
     states the smallest change it could have found, in the units
     of the business and as a share of a typical cell. It is
     reported whether or not anything cleared, because `nothing
     cleared` is precisely when a reader needs it.
